    description: "When auto-pr detects that the feature branch is behind base, it does:\n1. Snapshot .agent/tracker-workspace/.ops and .agent/tracker/.ops into /tmp/ops-backup-XXXXXX\n2. git rebase (which would normally wipe local .ops state)\n3. Restore the snapshot over the rebased working tree\n\nStep 3 silently overwrites any discuss entries posted AFTER step 1 but BEFORE step 3. Observed 2026-04-17: two tracker discuss WI-ripuz entries posted during the auto-pr run for PR #3110 vanished from the TUI mid-session — the user noticed their display of my comment disappear before their eyes. Confirmed via scripts/tracker show WI-ripuz: only the 2026-04-10 and 2026-04-14 entries remain; the 2026-04-17 entries are gone.\n\nRoot cause hypothesis: auto-pr does not replay tracker ops written during its own runtime. The backup snapshot is taken too early; anything the agent (or auto-sync) writes during CI polling is at risk.\n\nLikely fixes (not mutually exclusive):\n- Re-snapshot .ops just before the restore, not once at the start, and MERGE (union) the two snapshots rather than one-way restore.\n- Use Saved working directory and index state WIP on dev: 98ecb22ca feat(tracker): REPLY-FIRST CYCLE guidance when reply debt exists (WI-ripuz Phase 1) semantics rather than cp-based backup.\n- Disable auto-pr's ops snapshotting entirely when the tracker already has its own sync mechanism (tracker: sync PRs), and teach auto-pr to resolve .ops conflicts by union-merging instead.\n\nAlso exposes a secondary bug (filing separately): auto-pr exits 0 when the final merge does not complete but emits 'Recovery:' hints. Caller sees success, PR is not merged. Should be exit 1 or 2."  # 4022
    fields: {}  # 4022
